# OMA AI Cursor Orchestration

- Treat `@AGENTS.md` as the durable repository contract.
- At the start of each request, state one mode: `SETUP_ONLY`, `SPEC_ONLY`, `IMPLEMENT`, `BUG`, or `REVIEW`.
- Read the constitution and smallest relevant spec before proposing functional changes.
- For product-shell, UI, interaction, motion, or visual work, also read `@docs/DESIGN_REFERENCE_STRATEGY.md`; do not plan the base design system until `DEC-013` is approved.
- During initial setup, create only repository/tooling/spec/workflow files. Do not create product architecture or product code.
- Do not plan or implement while a blocker decision changes repository ownership, identity/tenant authority, security, external spend, or the affected integration.
- Inspect actual files, versions, authentication, scripts, tests, and dirty state before installing or changing tools.
- Use built-in Explore for noisy repository discovery and built-in Browser for browser work.
- Use `oma-spec-auditor` for independent scope/ownership review and `oma-verifier` for completion review.
- Start with zero subagents; use at most two for independent context-heavy work. Never fan out the same task.
- Use `inherit` models unless the user explicitly approves a pinned premium model/cost.
- Keep the parent accountable for handoffs, diff review, real checks, convergence, spec sync, and the final evidence report.
- Preserve OMA as an independent, original product under IMKAN. Do not copy IMKAN ONE or mix the visual systems of functional reference products.
- Never request or expose credentials in chat or files. Pause for the user's manual login when authentication is required.
